# ── Nothing personal belongs in this repository ─────────────────────────────
# This is the public half. Real threads, real briefs, real config and any
# credential live in the private data repo or in ~/.config/life-agent/.
# These patterns are a backstop, not the boundary — see docs/trust-model.md.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: unanchored `threads/` also matches
# `examples/threads/`, which silently excluded the synthetic fixtures the
# README and CI both depend on.
/threads/
/briefs/
/config.yaml
*.token
*.credentials.json
.env
.env.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
*.swp
